WEBVTT

00:10:25.463 --> 00:10:27.962
Look, dad's gone now.
We have to carry out his legacy.

00:10:27.996 --> 00:10:32.201
And that means hunting
down as many evil sons of
bitches as we possibly can.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:37.367
- Lisa.
- Dean.

00:10:37.414 --> 00:10:38.867
If you want to stick around
for a while,

00:10:38.914 --> 00:10:40.010
You're welcome to stay.

00:10:40.057 --> 00:10:43.771
I can't. I got a lot of work
to do, and it's not my life.

00:10:43.803 --> 00:10:45.399
Bela talbot's her real name.

00:10:45.423 --> 00:10:48.208
I procure unique items
for a select clientele.

00:10:48.232 --> 00:10:49.232
A thief.

00:10:49.255 --> 00:10:50.612
<I>A great thief.</I>

00:10:50.636 --> 00:10:53.517
Sam, you want to break
Dean free of that demon deal,

00:10:53.541 --> 00:10:55.327
You ain't gonna
find the answer in no book.

00:10:55.351 --> 00:10:58.208
- Then where, Bobby?
- Kid, I wish I knew.

00:10:58.232 --> 00:11:00.358
I've been busting my ass
trying to keep you alive, Dean,

00:11:00.382 --> 00:11:01.788
And you act like
you couldn't care less.

00:11:01.812 --> 00:11:03.977
<I>I don't want you
to worry about me, Dean.</I>

00:11:04.001 --> 00:11:05.644
<I>I want you
to worry about you.</I>

00:11:05.668 --> 00:11:07.788
I want you to give a crap
that you're dying.

00:11:07.812 --> 00:11:10.288
Every damn demon,
they were all human once?

00:11:10.334 --> 00:11:11.788
<I>Every one I've ever met.</I>

00:11:11.812 --> 00:11:14.533
The answer is yes,
by the way -- The same
thing will happen to you.

00:11:14.557 --> 00:11:17.676
There's no way of saving me
from the pit, is there?

00:11:17.699 --> 00:11:18.747
No.

00:11:21.914 --> 00:11:34.588
<font color="#ffff00">www.1000fr.com Presents</font>

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:51.381
<font color="#ffff00">Capture:Evelynzx
Sync:@FRS</font>

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.191
Oh. I'm sorry.

00:12:23.833 --> 00:12:25.405
Sir?

00:12:31.952 --> 00:12:33.857
Wake up.

00:12:38.531 --> 00:12:39.797
Wake up! You hear me?
Wake up!

00:12:40.984 --> 00:12:42.079
Sir, wake up!

00:12:42.103 --> 00:12:44.388
Help!
I need some help in here!

00:12:44.746 --> 00:12:50.330
Supernatural S03E10

00:13:08.269 --> 00:13:10.166
* down around the corner

00:13:10.213 --> 00:13:12.169
* half a mile from here

00:13:12.202 --> 00:13:13.870
* you see them long trains
runnin' *

00:13:13.903 --> 00:13:15.452
* and you watch them disappear

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:18.403
There you are.
What are you doing?

00:13:19.388 --> 00:13:21.460
Having a drink.

00:13:21.483 --> 00:13:23.626
It's 2:00 in the afternoon.
Drinking whiskey?

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.403
- I drink whiskey all the time.
- No, you don't.

00:13:25.436 --> 00:13:28.015
What's the big deal?
You get sloppy in bars.

00:13:28.062 --> 00:13:30.569
<I>You hit on chicks all the time.
Why can't I?</I>

00:13:32.848 --> 00:13:35.848
It's kind of slim pickings
around here.

00:13:35.872 --> 00:13:36.896
What's going on with you?

00:13:36.919 --> 00:13:38.569
* she lost her home
and her family *

00:13:38.603 --> 00:13:40.502
* and she won't be coming back

00:13:40.537 --> 00:13:42.269
* without love

00:13:42.302 --> 00:13:45.165
I tried, Dean.

00:13:45.189 --> 00:13:46.284
To do what?

00:13:46.308 --> 00:13:48.003
To save you.

00:13:52.235 --> 00:13:54.302
Can I get a whiskey?
Double, neat.

00:13:54.336 --> 00:13:56.522
- I'm serious, Dean.
- No, you're drunk.

00:13:56.547 --> 00:13:59.245
I mean,
where you're going...

00:13:59.292 --> 00:14:02.269
what you're gonna become.

00:14:04.135 --> 00:14:05.903
I can't stop it.

00:14:07.903 --> 00:14:11.037
I'm starting to think
maybe even ruby can't stop it.

00:14:12.903 --> 00:14:15.800
But, really, the thing is,
no one can save you.

00:14:15.823 --> 00:14:17.634
- What I've been telling you.
- No, that's not what I mean.

00:14:17.657 --> 00:14:21.466
I mean, no one can
save you because you
don't want to be saved.

00:14:22.252 --> 00:14:25.419
I mean, how can you care
so little about yourself?

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:29.803
What's wrong with you?

00:14:34.284 --> 00:14:36.522
Hello?

00:14:36.537 --> 00:14:38.603
Yes, this is
mr. Snyderson.

00:14:41.673 --> 00:14:43.864
What?

00:14:43.869 --> 00:14:45.336
Where?

00:14:52.204 --> 00:14:53.569
So, what's
the diagnosis?

00:14:53.604 --> 00:14:56.169
We've tested everything
we can think to test.

00:14:56.202 --> 00:14:57.918
He seems
perfectly healthy.

00:14:57.966 --> 00:14:59.013
Except that
he's comatose.

00:14:59.061 --> 00:15:02.369
Mr. Snyderson,
you're his emergency contact.

00:15:02.403 --> 00:15:04.703
Anything we should know?
Any illnesses?

00:15:04.736 --> 00:15:08.302
No, he never gets sick.
I mean, he doesn't even
catch a cold.

00:15:08.336 --> 00:15:11.473
Doctor, is there
anything you can do?

00:15:12.235 --> 00:15:13.783
Look, I'm sorry,

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.069
But we don't know
what's causing it,

00:15:16.116 --> 00:15:18.711
So we don't know
how to treat it.

00:15:18.736 --> 00:15:20.604
He just...

00:15:20.636 --> 00:15:24.169
went to sleep
and didn't wake up.

00:15:34.108 --> 00:15:36.537
So, what was Bobby doing
in pittsburgh?

00:15:36.585 --> 00:15:39.655
??

00:15:39.703 --> 00:15:42.751
???

00:15:42.917 --> 00:15:47.394
??

00:15:48.735 --> 00:15:50.496
???

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.996
??

00:15:55.187 --> 00:15:58.496
???

00:16:08.004 --> 00:16:10.147
??

00:16:13.624 --> 00:16:16.060
???

00:16:16.107 --> 00:16:19.155
??

00:16:22.037 --> 00:16:23.464
"Silene capensis,"

00:16:23.512 --> 00:16:26.321
<I>Which, of course, means
absolutely nothing to me.</I>

00:16:26.369 --> 00:16:28.107
??

00:16:28.759 --> 00:16:32.768
Dr. Walter gregg, 64,
university neurologist.

00:16:32.801 --> 00:16:34.101
How'd he bite it?

00:16:34.134 --> 00:16:35.639
Um, actually,
they don't know.

00:16:35.686 --> 00:16:38.663
They say he just went to sleep
and didn't wake up.

00:16:39.902 --> 00:16:42.242
That sound familiar
to you?

00:16:42.265 --> 00:16:44.671
All right, um...

00:16:44.694 --> 00:16:46.980
so, let's say Bobby was
looking into the doc's death,

00:16:47.004 --> 00:16:49.171
- You know,hunting after something...
- that started hunting him.

00:16:49.218 --> 00:16:50.265
Yeah.

00:16:50.289 --> 00:16:52.335
All right, stay here.
See if you can make
heads or tails of this.

00:16:52.368 --> 00:16:53.346
<I>What are you gonna do?</I>

00:16:53.393 --> 00:16:55.835
I'm gonna look into
the good doctor myself.

00:16:59.402 --> 00:17:02.101
So, you're
dr. Gregg's lab assistant.

00:17:02.134 --> 00:17:04.201
That's right.

00:17:04.234 --> 00:17:07.567
Well, his death must have
come as a shock to you.

00:17:07.601 --> 00:17:09.269
Yeah, it did.

00:17:09.301 --> 00:17:11.496
But, still,
go in your sleep, peaceful --

00:17:11.519 --> 00:17:12.996
It's what you wish for,
right?

00:17:13.019 --> 00:17:15.168
Yeah, right.

00:17:15.201 --> 00:17:19.043
Dr. Gregg, uh,
studied sleeping disorders?

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:20.567
Dreams?

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:21.519
I don't understand.

00:17:21.567 --> 00:17:23.503
I went over all of this
with the other detective.

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:24.980
You already spoke
to another detective?

00:17:25.028 --> 00:17:27.409
Yes, a very nice older man
with a beard.

00:17:27.432 --> 00:17:29.075
Well, I'd love to hear it again,
if you don't mind.

00:17:29.123 --> 00:17:32.836
Thing is, I'm sort of busy.
Maybe we could do this later?

00:17:33.435 --> 00:17:35.368
Sure. Yeah.

00:17:35.402 --> 00:17:37.893
I'll just bring you down to
the station later this afternoon

00:17:37.915 --> 00:17:41.320
And get your statement on tape,
do it all official-Like.

00:17:41.934 --> 00:17:45.320
Look, okay, I didn't know about
dr. Gregg's experiments --

00:17:45.345 --> 00:17:46.893
Not until I was
cleaning out his files.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:50.471
His experiments -- The ones
he was conducting on sleeping?

00:17:50.519 --> 00:17:53.768
No one knew, okay?
Not the university, not anybody.

00:17:54.519 --> 00:17:55.701
I already spoke
with a lawyer,

00:17:55.733 --> 00:17:58.967
And he told me that I can't
be held liable for anything.

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:00.637
T1maybe you couldn't,

00:18:00.662 --> 00:18:03.328
But that was before
the new evidence came to light.

00:18:03.375 --> 00:18:05.101
- New evidence?
- Mm-Hmm.

00:18:05.134 --> 00:18:06.502
What n evidence?

00:18:08.097 --> 00:18:10.170
I'm not at liberty
to say.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.813
Look,
I'm just a grad student.

00:18:12.836 --> 00:18:14.240
This was a gig
to cover tuition.

00:18:14.264 --> 00:18:17.240
Maybe so, but, still,
this -- This --

00:18:17.788 --> 00:18:20.605
This could go
on your permanent record.

00:18:20.634 --> 00:18:23.301
Unless you hand over
the doctor's research to me --

00:18:23.335 --> 00:18:25.177
All of it.

00:18:27.501 --> 00:18:29.567
Look, I don't know
what the r.A. Said,

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.351
But, uh,
I was growing ferns.

00:18:32.368 --> 00:18:34.400
Take it easy, phish.
That's not why I'm here.

00:18:34.423 --> 00:18:35.934
Really?

00:18:35.967 --> 00:18:38.041
Oh, thank god.
Okay.

00:18:38.066 --> 00:18:40.684
I want to talk to you
about dr. Gregg's sleep study.

00:18:40.708 --> 00:18:42.946
Yeah. Dr. Gregg
just died, right?

00:18:42.971 --> 00:18:44.351
You were one of
his test subjects, right?

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:45.979
Yeah.

00:18:48.811 --> 00:18:52.536
Ss you're on duty
or whatever.

00:18:54.644 --> 00:18:57.168
I guess
I can make an exception.

00:19:08.414 --> 00:19:10.368
Now, dr. Gregg
was testing treatments

00:19:10.402 --> 00:19:13.398
For a charcot-Wilbrand
syndrome,

00:19:13.423 --> 00:19:14.447
Which means...

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:17.588
um, I, uh,
I can't dream.

00:19:17.612 --> 00:19:20.065
I had this bike accident
when I was a kid,

00:19:20.088 --> 00:19:21.201
And I banged my head
pretty good,

00:19:21.255 --> 00:19:24.368
And I haven't
had a dream since.

00:19:25.112 --> 00:19:27.906
Till the study...
uh, sort of.

00:19:27.929 --> 00:19:28.788
What'd the doc give you?

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:31.001
It's this yellow tea.

00:19:31.025 --> 00:19:33.310
It smelled awful --
Tasted worse.

00:19:33.335 --> 00:19:34.144
What did it do?

00:19:34.192 --> 00:19:35.644
Just passed right out.

00:19:35.692 --> 00:19:40.961
And I had the most vivid,
super-Intense dream.

00:19:40.985 --> 00:19:42.366
Like a bad acid trip,
you know?

00:19:42.391 --> 00:19:43.835
Totally.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:45.366
I mean, no.

00:19:45.391 --> 00:19:46.699
That was it.

00:19:46.723 --> 00:19:48.675
I dropped out of his study
right after that.

00:19:48.699 --> 00:19:51.961
I didn't...like it.

00:19:51.985 --> 00:19:56.397
To tell you the truth...
it kind of scared me.

00:20:10.453 --> 00:20:12.286
How is he?

00:20:12.301 --> 00:20:14.239
No change.

00:20:14.262 --> 00:20:15.429
What you got?

00:20:15.476 --> 00:20:18.476
Well, considering
what you told me about
the doc's experiments,

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.889
Bobby's wall is
starting to make a hell
of a lot more sense.

00:20:20.913 --> 00:20:21.675
How so?

00:20:21.699 --> 00:20:23.222
This plant,
silene capensis,

00:20:23.246 --> 00:20:24.795
Also known as
african dream root,

00:20:24.817 --> 00:20:27.985
It's been used by shamen
and medicine men for centuries.

00:20:28.009 --> 00:20:30.722
Let me guess -- They dose up,
bust out the didgeridoos,

00:20:30.746 --> 00:20:32.175
And start kicking around
the hacky.

00:20:32.199 --> 00:20:33.152
Not quite.

00:20:33.175 --> 00:20:36.492
If you believe the legends,
it's used for dream-Walking.

00:20:36.516 --> 00:20:38.469
I mean, entering
another person's dreams,

00:20:38.492 --> 00:20:39.444
Poking around
in their heads.

00:20:39.469 --> 00:20:42.063
- I take it we believe the legends.
- When don't we?

00:20:42.087 --> 00:20:44.278
But dream-Walking is just
the tip of the iceberg.

00:20:44.302 --> 00:20:46.802
- What do you mean?
- I mean, this dream root is some serious mojo.

00:20:46.826 --> 00:20:48.380
You take enough of it,
with enough practice,

00:20:48.404 --> 00:20:50.429
You can become
a regular freddy krueger.

00:20:50.452 --> 00:20:51.501
You can control anything.

00:20:51.536 --> 00:20:53.952
You could
turn bad dreams good.

00:20:53.976 --> 00:20:55.643
You could
turn good dreams bad.

00:20:55.666 --> 00:20:57.904
And killing people
in their sleep.

00:20:57.929 --> 00:21:00.000
For example.

00:21:00.023 --> 00:21:01.626
So, let's say this doc

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.842
Was testing the stuff on
his patients tim leary-Style.

00:21:03.865 --> 00:21:05.134
Somebody
gets pissed at him,

00:21:05.168 --> 00:21:07.269
Decides to give him
a little dream visit,

00:21:07.301 --> 00:21:08.368
He goes nighty-Night.

00:21:08.402 --> 00:21:10.365
But what about Bobby?

00:21:10.389 --> 00:21:11.793
I mean, if the killer
came after him,

00:21:11.842 --> 00:21:14.368
How come
he's still alive?

00:21:14.402 --> 00:21:16.101
I don't know.

00:21:28.563 --> 00:21:30.237
Help me!

00:21:30.261 --> 00:21:32.101
Somebody help me!

00:21:32.134 --> 00:21:34.269
Help me!!

00:21:39.541 --> 00:21:42.000
So, how do we find
our homicidal little sandman?

00:21:42.023 --> 00:21:42.833
It could be anyone.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:43.746
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:21:43.793 --> 00:21:46.293
Anyone who knew the doctor,
had access to his dream shrooms.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:48.365
Maybe one of his test subjects
or something?

00:21:48.411 --> 00:21:50.435
Possible, but his research
is pretty sketchy.

00:21:50.483 --> 00:21:54.721
I mean, we don't know
how many subjects he had
or who all of them were.

00:21:55.197 --> 00:21:56.435
What?

00:21:56.467 --> 00:22:00.443
In any other case,we'd be calling Bobby And asking him for help right now.

00:22:00.490 --> 00:22:02.134
Know what?
You're right.

00:22:02.182 --> 00:22:04.752
- What?
- Let's go talk to him.

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:08.014
Sure. I think we might
find the conversation
a bit one-Sided.

00:22:08.063 --> 00:22:10.086
Not if we're tripping
on some dream root.

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:12.165
- What?
- You heard me.

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:14.041
You want to go dream-Walking
inside Bobby's head?

00:22:14.076 --> 00:22:15.047
Yeah, why not?
Maybe we could help.

00:22:15.094 --> 00:22:16.833
We have no idea what's
crawling around in there.

00:22:16.880 --> 00:22:19.308
- How bad could it be?
- Bad.

00:22:19.355 --> 00:22:21.474
Dude, it's Bobby.

00:22:23.403 --> 00:22:26.009
Yeah, you're right.

00:22:26.482 --> 00:22:29.315
One problem, though.We're fresh out of african dream root.

00:22:29.364 --> 00:22:32.650
Unless you know someone
who can score some...

00:22:32.697 --> 00:22:33.793
- Crap.
- What?

00:22:33.839 --> 00:22:35.601
Bela.
Bela?

00:22:35.650 --> 00:22:36.864
Crap.

00:22:38.101 --> 00:22:39.871
You're actually suggesting
we ask her for a favor?

00:22:39.918 --> 00:22:43.307
I'm feeling dirty just
thinking about it, but yeah.

00:23:04.617 --> 00:23:06.862
Hey, Sam.

00:23:06.886 --> 00:23:08.077
Bela.

00:23:08.125 --> 00:23:10.054
I didn't think there was
a chance in hell you'd show up.

00:23:10.101 --> 00:23:12.407
Well,
I'm full of surprises.

00:23:12.839 --> 00:23:16.934
Though, truthfully,
you want to know why I'm here?

00:23:16.981 --> 00:23:18.886
Okay.

00:23:18.911 --> 00:23:21.251
Because of you.

00:23:23.038 --> 00:23:24.299
Uh, what are you doing?

00:23:24.346 --> 00:23:25.965
I can't stop
thinking about you.

00:23:26.014 --> 00:23:27.965
What?

00:23:31.418 --> 00:23:33.107
Are you sure?

00:23:36.442 --> 00:23:37.259
Sam.

00:23:37.307 --> 00:23:38.211
Sam.

00:23:38.259 --> 00:23:39.307
Sam. Oh.

00:23:39.355 --> 00:23:42.009
Sam, wake up!

00:23:49.541 --> 00:23:51.266
Dude, you were out.

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:53.315
And making
some serious happy noises.

00:23:53.338 --> 00:23:54.541
Who were you
dreaming about?

00:23:54.574 --> 00:23:56.458
- What?
- No one. Nothing.

00:23:56.481 --> 00:23:58.076
Come on. You can tell me.
Angelina jolie?

00:23:58.107 --> 00:23:59.076
No.

00:23:59.107 --> 00:24:00.536
- Brad pitt?
- No! 

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:01.918
No.

00:24:01.942 --> 00:24:03.041
Dude, it doesn't matter.

00:24:03.076 --> 00:24:05.155
- Whatever.
- Whatever.

00:24:05.203 --> 00:24:07.107
I called Bela.

00:24:08.918 --> 00:24:11.141
Bela? Yeah?

00:24:11.174 --> 00:24:15.174
W-What'd she, you know,
say?

00:24:15.208 --> 00:24:17.442
She's...gonna...help us?

00:24:17.474 --> 00:24:20.608
Shockingly, no, which puts us
back to square one.

00:24:20.641 --> 00:24:22.831
I've been trying to decipher
the doctor's notes.

00:24:22.877 --> 00:24:26.107
<I>Unfortunately, he has
worse handwriting than you do.</I>

00:24:27.407 --> 00:24:29.741
You gonna come help me
with this stuff?

00:24:31.290 --> 00:24:34.541
Yeah, yeah.
Just give me a sec.

00:24:49.240 --> 00:24:51.275
Bela,
as I live and breathe.

00:24:51.322 --> 00:24:54.250
You called me,
remember?

00:24:54.275 --> 00:24:55.942
I remember
you turning me down.

00:24:55.976 --> 00:24:58.711
Well, I'm just
full of surprises.

00:24:58.735 --> 00:25:00.806
Hey, Bela.
What's going on?

00:25:00.829 --> 00:25:03.474
I brought you
your african dream root.

00:25:03.507 --> 00:25:07.139
Nasty stuff.
And not easy to come by.

00:25:07.163 --> 00:25:08.775
Why the sudden
change of heart?

00:25:08.808 --> 00:25:11.842
What, I can't do
you a little favor
every now and again?

00:25:11.875 --> 00:25:14.076
No, you're not.

00:25:14.098 --> 00:25:17.342
Now, come on. I want to
know what the strings are
before you attach 'em.

00:25:17.375 --> 00:25:20.009
You said this was
for Bobby singer, right?

00:25:20.041 --> 00:25:23.106
<I>Well, I'm doing it for him,
not you.</I>

00:25:23.130 --> 00:25:24.273
Bobby?

00:25:24.298 --> 00:25:26.179
Why?

00:25:26.608 --> 00:25:30.608
He saved my life once...
in flagstaff.

00:25:32.842 --> 00:25:36.781
I screwed up, and he saved me,
okay? Are you satisfied?

00:25:36.808 --> 00:25:38.947
Maybe.

00:25:38.971 --> 00:25:41.685
So, when do we go on this little
magical mystery tour?

00:25:41.710 --> 00:25:43.353
<I>Oh, you're
not going anywhere.</I>

00:25:43.376 --> 00:25:45.041
<I>I don't trust you enough
to let you in my car,</I>

00:25:45.076 --> 00:25:47.174
Much less Bobby's head.

00:25:47.208 --> 00:25:48.875
No offense.

00:25:50.407 --> 00:25:53.193
None taken.

00:25:54.980 --> 00:25:56.842
It's 2:00 a.M.
Where am I supposed to go?

00:25:56.875 --> 00:25:58.741
Get a room.

00:25:58.764 --> 00:26:00.645
Oh, they got
the magic fingers,

00:26:00.670 --> 00:26:02.193
A little "casa erotica"
on pay-Per-View.

00:26:02.217 --> 00:26:03.217
You'll love it.

00:26:03.241 --> 00:26:04.507
You...

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:08.367
nice to -- S-Seeing you...

00:26:08.891 --> 00:26:10.797
...Bela.

00:26:18.994 --> 00:26:20.232
Well,
shall we dim t lights

00:26:20.257 --> 00:26:23.804
And sync up "wizard of oz"
and "dark side of the moon"?

00:26:23.842 --> 00:26:26.019
Why?

00:26:26.041 --> 00:26:28.661
What did you do
during college?

00:26:28.708 --> 00:26:30.842
Wait, wait, wait.
Whew.

00:26:30.875 --> 00:26:32.641
Can't forget this.

00:26:33.741 --> 00:26:36.170
Here.

00:26:36.192 --> 00:26:37.192
What the hell is that?

00:26:37.217 --> 00:26:39.264
Bobby's hair.

00:26:39.288 --> 00:26:40.674
We have to drink
Bobby's hair?

00:26:40.708 --> 00:26:42.217
That's how you control
whose dream you're entering.

00:26:42.264 --> 00:26:45.541
You got to drink
some of their, uh...

00:26:45.574 --> 00:26:48.201
some of their body.

00:26:48.808 --> 00:26:50.605
Well, guess
the hair of the dog's

00:26:50.641 --> 00:26:52.608
<I>Better than
other parts of the body.</I>

00:26:54.605 --> 00:26:56.407
- Bottoms up.
- Yeah.

00:27:09.636 --> 00:27:11.541
Feel anything?

00:27:12.494 --> 00:27:13.954
No.

00:27:13.978 --> 00:27:16.174
<I>You feel anything?</I>

00:27:16.208 --> 00:27:18.407
No.

00:27:18.442 --> 00:27:21.692
Maybe we got
some bad schwag.

00:27:23.096 --> 00:27:25.478
Hey, when did it
start raining?

00:27:37.207 --> 00:27:40.107
<I>When did it start raining
upside down?</I>

00:27:51.065 --> 00:27:52.183
Okay, I don't know
what's weirder --

00:27:52.231 --> 00:27:54.741
The fact
that we're in Bobby's head

00:27:54.774 --> 00:27:56.841
<I>Or that he's dreaming
of better homes and gardens.</I>

00:27:56.883 --> 00:27:58.167
Wait.
Wait a second.

00:27:58.215 --> 00:28:00.442
Imagine the place
without the paint job,

00:28:00.474 --> 00:28:05.808
More cluttered, dusty,
books all over the place.

00:28:06.453 --> 00:28:07.442
It's Bobby's house.

00:28:07.474 --> 00:28:09.174
Yeah.

00:28:09.208 --> 00:28:11.057
Bobby?

00:28:25.254 --> 00:28:27.206
Bobby?

00:28:30.469 --> 00:28:31.754
Dean.

00:28:33.739 --> 00:28:34.875
I'm gonna go
look outside.

00:28:34.908 --> 00:28:36.274
No, no, no.
Stay close.

00:28:36.307 --> 00:28:38.841
Dude, I'll be fine.
Just look around in here.

00:28:38.875 --> 00:28:41.119
Look,
we got to find him.

00:28:41.144 --> 00:28:43.857
Don't do anything stupid.

00:29:12.975 --> 00:29:14.442
Dean!

00:29:20.875 --> 00:29:22.575
Dean!

00:29:40.373 --> 00:29:41.908
Bobby?

00:29:46.841 --> 00:29:48.608
Bobby?!

00:29:54.741 --> 00:29:57.107
Who's out there?

00:30:03.595 --> 00:30:04.774
Bobby, you in there?

00:30:05.427 --> 00:30:06.238
Dean?

00:30:06.260 --> 00:30:08.107
Yeah, it's me.
Open up.

00:30:08.141 --> 00:30:09.547
Hey.

00:30:12.244 --> 00:30:13.792
How the hell
did you find me?

00:30:13.817 --> 00:30:16.482
Sam and I got our hands on
some of that dream-Root stuff.

00:30:16.507 --> 00:30:18.197
Drearoot? What?

00:30:18.221 --> 00:30:20.317
Dr. Gregg --
The experiments?

00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:22.769
What the hell
are you talking about?

00:30:23.173 --> 00:30:23.912
Hurry.

00:30:23.960 --> 00:30:26.141
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.What's going on?
- She's coming.

00:30:26.174 --> 00:30:28.375
Okay, you know
this is a dream, don't you?

00:30:28.420 --> 00:30:29.682
W-Whate you crazy?

00:30:29.729 --> 00:30:31.895
It's a dream, Bobby.
None of this is real.

00:30:31.920 --> 00:30:34.009
Does that look made up?

00:30:36.207 --> 00:30:37.541
No.

00:30:40.737 --> 00:30:43.594
Bobby, who is that?

00:30:43.617 --> 00:30:45.165
She's...

00:30:45.189 --> 00:30:47.307
she's my wife.

00:31:09.892 --> 00:31:12.133
Why, Bobby?

00:31:12.156 --> 00:31:14.892
Why did you do this
to me?

00:31:17.918 --> 00:31:20.258
I'd have rather died myself
than hurt you.

00:31:20.290 --> 00:31:22.951
<I>But you did hurt me.</I>

00:31:22.973 --> 00:31:26.023
You shoved that knife
into me...

00:31:26.057 --> 00:31:29.258
again and again.

00:31:30.355 --> 00:31:33.021
You watched me bleed...

00:31:33.046 --> 00:31:35.243
watched me die.

00:31:35.268 --> 00:31:36.934
Bobby, she's not real.

00:31:36.981 --> 00:31:38.957
How could you?

00:31:39.743 --> 00:31:42.195
You were possessed,
baby.

00:31:42.223 --> 00:31:43.490
You were rabid.

00:31:43.524 --> 00:31:45.758
And I didn't know
what I know now.

00:31:45.790 --> 00:31:47.625
I didn't know
how to save you.

00:31:47.657 --> 00:31:51.085
<I>You're lying.
You wanted me dead.</I>

00:31:51.108 --> 00:31:53.276
If you'd loved me,
you would have found a way!!

00:31:53.298 --> 00:31:55.728
- I'm sorry.
- Come on.

00:32:07.998 --> 00:32:10.259
- Who are you?
- Who are you?

00:32:10.282 --> 00:32:11.282
You don't belong here.

00:32:11.357 --> 00:32:13.758
You're one to talk.
You're in my friend's head.

00:32:13.790 --> 00:32:15.480
Well, you got a poor choice
in friends.

00:32:15.528 --> 00:32:19.147
This is self-Defense.
He came after me.
H-He wanted to hurt me.

00:32:19.172 --> 00:32:21.742
That may be
because you're a killer.

00:32:21.767 --> 00:32:24.090
You should be nicer
to me.

00:32:24.124 --> 00:32:27.490
In here,
you're just an insect.

00:32:27.524 --> 00:32:28.790
I'm a god.

00:32:30.691 --> 00:32:33.155
I'm telling you -- All of it,
your house, your wife --

00:32:33.202 --> 00:32:35.023
It's a nightmare.

00:32:38.290 --> 00:32:40.163
I killed her.
Boby

00:32:40.211 --> 00:32:42.686
This is a dream and you can wake up.

00:32:42.734 --> 00:32:44.402
<I>Hell,
you can do anything.</I>

00:32:44.424 --> 00:32:47.472
Just leave me alone.
Let her kill me already.

00:32:47.520 --> 00:32:48.758
Look at me.
Look at me.

00:32:48.806 --> 00:32:49.949
You got to
snap out of this now.

00:32:49.997 --> 00:32:51.524
You got to
snap out of this now!

00:32:51.557 --> 00:32:53.045
You're not gonna die.
I'm not gonna let you die.

00:32:53.091 --> 00:32:55.825
I'm not gonna let nnu die.
You're like a father to me.

00:32:56.814 --> 00:32:58.758
You've got to believe me.Please!

00:33:03.124 --> 00:33:04.051
I'm dreaming?

00:33:04.076 --> 00:33:06.773
Yes!
Now, take control of it!

00:33:26.901 --> 00:33:29.067
I don't believe it.

00:33:31.615 --> 00:33:34.353
Believe it.

00:33:35.067 --> 00:33:36.718
Now,
would you please wake up?

00:33:36.741 --> 00:33:38.336
Sweet dreams.

00:33:54.534 --> 00:33:57.201
Hey, Bobby...

00:33:57.225 --> 00:34:02.399
that, uh, that stuff --
All that stuff with your wife...

00:34:03.637 --> 00:34:06.567
...that actually happen?

00:34:08.710 --> 00:34:12.090
<I>Everybody got into hunting
somehow.</I>

00:34:13.137 --> 00:34:13.923
I'm sorry.

00:34:13.947 --> 00:34:15.670
Don't be sorry.

00:34:15.693 --> 00:34:17.979
If it weren't for you,
I'd still be lost in there...

00:34:18.145 --> 00:34:20.122
or dead.

00:34:21.956 --> 00:34:24.313
Thank you.

00:34:31.130 --> 00:34:33.510
So, uh, stoner boy
wasn't in his dorm.

00:34:33.534 --> 00:34:35.248
My guess is
he's long gone by now.

00:34:35.273 --> 00:34:36.653
He ain't
much of a stoner.

00:34:36.701 --> 00:34:38.416
- No?
- No.

00:34:38.462 --> 00:34:42.701
His name's jeremy frost --
Full-On genius -- 160 I.Q.

00:34:42.748 --> 00:34:43.987
Which is saying something,

00:34:44.010 --> 00:34:47.114
Considering his dad took
a baseball bat to his head.

00:34:47.257 --> 00:34:50.208
Here's
father of the year.

00:34:50.233 --> 00:34:51.851
He died
before jeremy was 10.

00:34:51.876 --> 00:34:52.899
Looks like
a real sweetheart.

00:34:52.922 --> 00:34:54.994
Injury gave him
charcot-Wilbrand.

00:34:55.019 --> 00:34:56.233
He hasn't dreamt since.

00:34:56.280 --> 00:34:58.257
Till he started
dosing the dream drug.
Yep.

00:34:58.280 --> 00:34:59.733
yep.

00:34:59.757 --> 00:35:02.788
How did he know how to
dig up your worst nightmare
and throw it at you?

00:35:02.811 --> 00:35:04.550
Hey, he was rooting around
in my skull.

00:35:04.574 --> 00:35:05.931
God knows
what he saw in there.

00:35:05.954 --> 00:35:07.574
Yeah, how'd he get in there
in the first place?

00:35:07.597 --> 00:35:09.550
Isn't he supposed to
have some of your hair,
your dna, or something?

00:35:09.574 --> 00:35:11.622
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:35:11.676 --> 00:35:14.914
Before I knew it was him,
he offered me a beer.

00:35:14.938 --> 00:35:16.819
I drank it.

00:35:16.844 --> 00:35:19.105
Dumbest friggin' thing.

00:35:19.844 --> 00:35:22.201
Oh, I don't know.
It wasn't that dumb.

00:35:23.724 --> 00:35:25.081
Dean, you didn't.

00:35:25.088 --> 00:35:25.850
I was thirsty.

00:35:25.898 --> 00:35:27.970
That's great. Now he can
come after either one of you.

00:35:27.993 --> 00:35:30.136
<I>Well, now we just have to
find him first.</I>

00:35:30.161 --> 00:35:33.993
We better work fast...
and coffee up.

00:35:34.018 --> 00:35:36.850
<I>'Cause the one thing
we cannot do is fall asleep.</I>

00:35:36.898 --> 00:35:40.184
Two days later.

00:35:41.810 --> 00:35:43.501
I mean, this jeremy guy's
not a friggin' ghost.

00:35:43.525 --> 00:35:46.310
Where the hell
could he be?

00:35:46.335 --> 00:35:47.431
Dean, you sure
you don't want me to drive?

00:35:47.478 --> 00:35:49.644
You -- You seem
a little...caffeinated.

00:35:49.668 --> 00:35:52.407
Well, thanks for
the news flash, edison!

00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:56.938
Jeez.

00:35:56.961 --> 00:35:58.128
Tell me
you got something!

00:35:58.153 --> 00:36:01.224
- The strip club was a bust, huh?
- Yeah.

00:36:01.248 --> 00:36:02.795
That was our last lead.

00:36:02.818 --> 00:36:03.945
What the hell, Bobby?!

00:36:03.970 --> 00:36:05.398
Don't yell at me, boy.

00:36:05.422 --> 00:36:07.541
- I'm working my ass off here.
- Sorry. I'm sorry.

00:36:07.565 --> 00:36:08.778
I'm just --
I'm -- I'm tired.

00:36:08.802 --> 00:36:09.755
Well, who ain't?

00:36:09.778 --> 00:36:11.493
What's Bela got?

00:36:11.516 --> 00:36:13.708
What do you got, Bela?
Sorry.

00:36:13.731 --> 00:36:15.684
Sometimes the spirit world's
in a chatty mood,

00:36:15.708 --> 00:36:17.327
And sometimes it isn't.

00:36:17.350 --> 00:36:18.659
- She's got nothing.
- Great!

00:36:18.684 --> 00:36:22.619
Well, I'm just gonna go
blow my brains out now!

00:36:22.667 --> 00:36:24.262
??

00:36:29.739 --> 00:36:32.358
Let me ask you something.

00:36:32.382 --> 00:36:35.176
What are you doing
helping us?

00:36:35.211 --> 00:36:39.032
Bobby, I'm surprised
you don't remember.

00:36:39.056 --> 00:36:41.461
Flagstaff?

00:36:42.278 --> 00:36:43.841
Oh.

00:36:43.865 --> 00:36:45.278
Yeah.

00:36:45.310 --> 00:36:47.627
Right.

00:36:48.509 --> 00:36:51.010
Flagstaff.

00:37:06.523 --> 00:37:08.809
All right, that's it.
I'm done.

00:37:09.643 --> 00:37:10.382
What are you doing?

00:37:10.404 --> 00:37:12.047
Taking myself
a long-Overdue nap.

00:37:12.072 --> 00:37:13.976
What? Dean,
jeremy can come after you.

00:37:14.023 --> 00:37:15.077
That's the idea.

00:37:15.110 --> 00:37:16.047
Excuse me?

00:37:16.096 --> 00:37:18.532
<I>Co on, man. We can't find him,
so let him come to me.</I>

00:37:18.579 --> 00:37:20.936
On his own turf --
Where he's basically a god?

00:37:20.961 --> 00:37:23.199
I can handle it.

00:37:23.222 --> 00:37:24.443
Not alone you can't.

00:37:24.476 --> 00:37:25.818
Ow!

00:37:25.864 --> 00:37:27.104
What are you doing?

00:37:27.150 --> 00:37:28.150
Coming in with you.

00:37:28.175 --> 00:37:30.077
- No, you're not.
- Why not?

00:37:30.110 --> 00:37:33.730
At least then,
it'll be two against one.

00:37:34.301 --> 00:37:35.911
'Cause I don't want you
digging around in my head.

00:37:35.943 --> 00:37:38.349
Too bad.

00:37:51.904 --> 00:37:53.856
Dean.

00:37:56.213 --> 00:37:59.030
For the love of god.

00:38:00.030 --> 00:38:01.746
What are we
still doing here?

00:38:01.769 --> 00:38:04.435
I have no idea.

00:38:07.555 --> 00:38:10.317
There's someone
out there.

00:38:24.974 --> 00:38:30.278
* stars shining bright
above you *

00:38:30.310 --> 00:38:34.876
* night breezes
seem to whisper "I love you" *

00:38:34.911 --> 00:38:36.617
Hey.

00:38:36.641 --> 00:38:38.784
You gonna sit down?

00:38:39.958 --> 00:38:41.507
Come on.

00:38:41.530 --> 00:38:42.377
We only have an hour

00:38:42.435 --> 00:38:45.777
Before we have to pick ben up
from baseball.

00:38:46.530 --> 00:38:50.149
* say nighty-Night and kiss me

00:38:50.173 --> 00:38:52.134
I've never had this dream
before.

00:38:52.157 --> 00:38:56.077
* just hold me tight
and tell me you'll miss me *

00:38:56.110 --> 00:38:59.204
Stop looking at me
like that.

00:38:59.229 --> 00:38:59.918
Sorry.

00:38:59.943 --> 00:39:01.538
Dean.

00:39:02.943 --> 00:39:05.443
I love you.

00:39:13.094 --> 00:39:15.260
Where'd she go?

00:39:17.380 --> 00:39:19.188
Dean.

00:39:39.871 --> 00:39:42.061
 Okay.

00:39:57.735 --> 00:39:59.878
Dean?

00:40:29.234 --> 00:40:31.711
Jeremy?

00:40:47.837 --> 00:40:49.791
Hey, Dean.

00:40:55.846 --> 00:40:58.632
Well, aren't you
a handsome son of a gun.

00:40:58.655 --> 00:41:00.559
We need to talk.

00:41:00.583 --> 00:41:02.618
I get it. I get it.

00:41:02.652 --> 00:41:04.655
I'm my own
worst nightmare.

00:41:04.702 --> 00:41:06.274
That it? Huh?

00:41:06.322 --> 00:41:08.226
Like the "superman iii"
junkyard scene --

00:41:08.274 --> 00:41:10.782
A little mano y mano
with myself?

00:41:10.829 --> 00:41:13.585
Joke all you want,
smartass.

00:41:14.711 --> 00:41:16.139
<I>But you can't lie to me.</I>

00:41:16.186 --> 00:41:18.259
I know the truth.

00:41:18.306 --> 00:41:20.639
I know how dead you are
inside...

00:41:20.686 --> 00:41:22.972
how worthless
you feel.

00:41:23.019 --> 00:41:26.576
I know how
you look into a mirror...

00:41:26.623 --> 00:41:29.456
and hate what you see.

00:41:30.789 --> 00:41:34.086
Sorry, pal.
It's not gonna work.

00:41:34.118 --> 00:41:35.123
You're not real.

00:41:35.171 --> 00:41:37.456
Sure I am.

00:41:37.480 --> 00:41:38.179
I'm you.

00:41:38.225 --> 00:41:40.725
I don't think so.

00:41:40.750 --> 00:41:43.250
<I>'Cause, see,
this is my siesta...</I>

00:41:43.273 --> 00:41:44.725
not yours.

00:41:44.773 --> 00:41:48.679
All I got to do is snap
my fingers, and you go bye-Bye.

00:41:59.639 --> 00:42:01.925
I'm not going anywhere.

00:42:01.971 --> 00:42:03.805
Neither are you.

00:42:08.123 --> 00:42:10.550
Like I said...

00:42:10.599 --> 00:42:11.574
we need to talk.

00:42:15.099 --> 00:42:17.336
Dean.

00:42:17.623 --> 00:42:19.320
Hey.

00:42:19.345 --> 00:42:21.868
Wake up.

00:42:27.868 --> 00:42:31.305
Boy, you just don't know
When to leave well enough
alone, do you?

00:42:31.328 --> 00:42:32.452
You're a psycho.

00:42:32.484 --> 00:42:33.710
- You're wrong.
- Yeah?

00:42:33.733 --> 00:42:35.685
Tell that to dr. Gregg.

00:42:35.719 --> 00:42:37.418
The doc?

00:42:37.452 --> 00:42:39.780
No, no, the doc's the one
who got me hooked on this stuff,

00:42:39.828 --> 00:42:41.851
And then he took it away.

00:42:41.876 --> 00:42:43.284
But I needed it,

00:42:43.328 --> 00:42:45.153
And he wouldn't
let me have it.

00:42:45.184 --> 00:42:46.719
So you killed him.

00:42:46.751 --> 00:42:48.952
I can dream again.

00:42:48.985 --> 00:42:52.764
You know what that's like --
Not to be able to dream?

00:42:52.813 --> 00:42:54.336
Y-You never rest --
Not really.

00:42:54.384 --> 00:42:57.407
I-It's like being awake
for 15 years.

00:42:57.454 --> 00:42:59.764
And let me guess --
That makes you go crazy.

00:42:59.813 --> 00:43:02.914
I just want
to be left alone.

00:43:02.938 --> 00:43:05.081
I just want to dream.

00:43:05.130 --> 00:43:06.519
Sorry.

00:43:06.551 --> 00:43:08.019
Can't do that.

00:43:08.052 --> 00:43:10.153
That's the wrong answer.

00:43:21.208 --> 00:43:24.318
I'm getting better and better
at this --

00:43:24.351 --> 00:43:27.597
Stronger and stronger
all the time.

00:43:29.193 --> 00:43:31.184
But you
and your brother...

00:43:31.217 --> 00:43:33.719
you're not waking up...

00:43:33.751 --> 00:43:35.954
not this time.

00:43:35.979 --> 00:43:37.358
I'm not gonna let you.

00:43:37.382 --> 00:43:39.019
I mean,
you're going to hell,

00:43:39.052 --> 00:43:40.907
And you won't lift a finger
to stop it.

00:43:40.954 --> 00:43:43.414
Talk about low self-Esteem.

00:43:43.461 --> 00:43:46.296
Then, again, I guess
it's not much of a life
worth saving, now, is it?

00:43:46.342 --> 00:43:47.367
Come on, Dean.
Come on. Wake up.

00:43:47.414 --> 00:43:51.319
??

00:43:51.342 --> 00:43:52.885
<I>You are nothing.</I>

00:43:53.891 --> 00:43:56.452
You're as mindless and obedient
as an attack dog.

00:43:56.484 --> 00:43:58.452
- That's not true.
- No?

00:43:59.945 --> 00:44:01.755
What are the things
that you want?

00:44:01.779 --> 00:44:04.518
What are the things
that you dream?

00:44:04.541 --> 00:44:07.136
I mean, your car --
That's dad's.

00:44:07.161 --> 00:44:08.978
Your favorite
leather jacket -- Dad's.

00:44:09.001 --> 00:44:10.835
Your music -- Dad's.

00:44:10.858 --> 00:44:14.215
<I>Do you even have
an original thought?</I>

00:44:14.239 --> 00:44:15.335
No.

00:44:15.358 --> 00:44:17.478
No, all there is
is "watch out for Sammy.

00:44:17.501 --> 00:44:20.953
Look after
your little brother, boy."

00:44:21.024 --> 00:44:24.127
You can still hear your dad's
voice in your head, can't you?

00:44:24.152 --> 00:44:25.056
Clear as a bell.

00:44:25.105 --> 00:44:27.032
Just shut up.

00:44:28.413 --> 00:44:30.438
I mean, think about it.

00:44:30.461 --> 00:44:33.175
All he ever d
was train you...

00:44:33.199 --> 00:44:35.605
boss you around.

00:44:35.628 --> 00:44:37.445
But Sam...

00:44:37.492 --> 00:44:39.849
Sam, he doted on.

00:44:39.873 --> 00:44:40.826
Sam, he loved.

00:44:40.849 --> 00:44:42.802
I mean it.
I'm getting angry.

00:44:42.826 --> 00:44:45.565
Dad knew
who you really were --

00:44:45.588 --> 00:44:48.945
A good soldier
and nothing else.

00:44:48.969 --> 00:44:51.762
Daddy's
blunt little instrument.

00:44:51.786 --> 00:44:54.311
Your own father didn't care
whether you lived or died.

00:44:54.333 --> 00:44:57.668
- Why should you?
- You son of a bitch!

00:44:57.690 --> 00:45:00.262
My father
was an obsessed bastard!

00:45:03.985 --> 00:45:06.485
All that crap he dumped on me
about protecting Sam --

00:45:06.509 --> 00:45:07.722
<I>That was his crap!</I>

00:45:07.746 --> 00:45:10.793
<I>He's thalone who couldn
protect his family!</I>

00:45:11.628 --> 00:45:13.532
He's the one
who let mom die!

00:45:13.556 --> 00:45:16.063
<I>Who wasn't there for Sam!
I always was!</I>

00:45:16.088 --> 00:45:17.016
It wasn't fair!

00:45:17.039 --> 00:45:18.920
I didn't deserve
what he put on me!

00:45:18.945 --> 00:45:21.088
And I don't deserve
to go to hell!

00:45:48.413 --> 00:45:51.351
You can't escape me, Dean.
You're gonna die.

00:45:51.384 --> 00:45:55.221
<I>And this -- This is
what you're gonna become.</I>

00:45:55.246 --> 00:45:58.056
You can't stop me.

00:45:58.079 --> 00:46:00.181
There's nothing
I can't do in here.

00:46:00.206 --> 00:46:01.659
Because of
the dream root.

00:46:01.681 --> 00:46:02.896
That's right.

00:46:02.943 --> 00:46:05.920
Yeah? Well,
you're forgetting something.

00:46:05.943 --> 00:46:08.706
What's tha

00:46:09.824 --> 00:46:12.547
I took the dream root,
too.

00:46:12.570 --> 00:46:13.976
Jeremy?!

00:46:14.000 --> 00:46:16.333
Jeremy!

00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:18.713
No.

00:46:18.737 --> 00:46:20.927
No.

00:46:20.951 --> 00:46:21.690
Dad?

00:46:21.713 --> 00:46:24.570
You answer me
when I'm talking to you, boy!

00:46:50.498 --> 00:46:53.641
You did a little dream-Weaving
of your own in there, huh?

00:46:53.664 --> 00:46:55.737
Yeah, uh, I just
sort of concentrated,

00:46:55.764 --> 00:46:57.297
And it happened,
you know?

00:46:57.355 --> 00:46:59.831
Didn't have anything
to do with...

00:46:59.864 --> 00:47:03.617
you know,
your psychic stuff?

00:47:06.601 --> 00:47:08.697
No.

00:47:08.744 --> 00:47:11.577
I mean,
I don't think so.

00:47:12.172 --> 00:47:13.125
Good.

00:47:13.150 --> 00:47:14.768
Good.

00:47:21.467 --> 00:47:22.918
Hey,
you guys seen Bela?

00:47:22.942 --> 00:47:25.561
She's not in her room.
She's not answering her phone.

00:47:26.324 --> 00:47:28.394
She must have taken off
or something.

00:47:28.418 --> 00:47:29.657
Just like that?
That's a little weird.

00:47:29.681 --> 00:47:33.181
Well, if you ask me what's
weird, it's why she helped
us in the first place.

00:47:33.204 --> 00:47:35.355
I thought
you saved her life.

00:47:35.378 --> 00:47:37.474
What the hell
are you talking about?

00:47:37.498 --> 00:47:40.402
The thing flagstaff.

00:47:40.427 --> 00:47:43.284
That thing in flagstaff
was an amulet.

00:47:43.307 --> 00:47:46.188
I gave her a good deal.
That's all.

00:47:47.530 --> 00:47:49.672
Well, then, why did --

00:47:49.697 --> 00:47:53.172
You boys better check
your pockets.

00:47:53.197 --> 00:47:55.338
??

00:47:58.648 --> 00:48:00.530
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:48:02.942 --> 00:48:04.657
The colt.

00:48:05.371 --> 00:48:07.157
Bela stole the colt.

00:48:07.179 --> 00:48:08.918
Damn it, boys!

00:48:08.942 --> 00:48:10.632
Pack your crap.

00:48:10.657 --> 00:48:12.132
Why?
Where are we going?

00:48:12.179 --> 00:48:15.061
We're gonna go
hunt the bitch down.

00:48:17.925 --> 00:48:20.378
Hey, Sam,
I was wondering --

00:48:20.402 --> 00:48:22.331
When you were in my head,
what did you see?

00:48:22.355 --> 00:48:25.806
Uh, just jeremy.
He kept me separated from you.

00:48:25.831 --> 00:48:28.782
Easier to beat my brains out
that way, I guess.

00:48:28.806 --> 00:48:31.266
What about you?
You never said.

00:48:31.291 --> 00:48:34.264
<I>Nothing. I was looking for you
the whole time.</I>

00:48:42.704 --> 00:48:43.893
Sam...

00:48:43.918 --> 00:48:45.346
yeah?

00:48:45.775 --> 00:48:48.846
I've been doing
some thinking.

00:48:48.869 --> 00:48:51.565
And...

00:48:52.108 --> 00:48:54.132
well, the thing is...

00:48:56.442 --> 00:49:00.306
...I don't want to die.

00:49:02.045 --> 00:49:05.735
I don't want
to go to hell.

00:49:08.972 --> 00:49:11.409
All right, yeah.

00:49:11.432 --> 00:49:14.742
We'll find a way
to save you.

00:49:16.480 --> 00:49:18.052
Okay, good.

00:49:20.670 --> 00:49:22.456
You n't escape me, Dean.

00:49:22.480 --> 00:49:24.012
You're gonna die.

00:49:24.036 --> 00:49:26.846
<I>And this -- This is
what you're gonna become.</I>

